  {
   "id": "m-hP73dRC48J",
   "from": "Allan Just",
   "author": "13ff1921a4b26560",
   "date": "2014-10-30T01:39:58Z",
   "subject": "Re: ggplot legend disappears when geom_title counter is over 260",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Rares,</div><div>  can you provide a reproducible example? Otherwise we can&#39;t tell what you are trying to do. Here is a geom_tile plot with 261 discrete values for fill in the legend:</div><div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">library(ggplot2)</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">mydf &lt;- data.frame(x = 1, y = factor(1:261))</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">ggplot(mydf, aes(x, y)) + geom_tile(aes(fill = y))</font></div></div><div><br></div><div>#R 3.1.1; ggplot2_1.0.0</div><div>-Allan</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Tuesday, October 28, 2014 6:33:20 PM UTC-4, Rares Vernica wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<br><br>I get a very strange behavior out of ggplot and geom_title. The legend disappears if the fill counter is over 260. Here is the code:<br><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(29,31,33)\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;line-height:1.25;white-space:pre-wrap!important;outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;font-size:10pt!important\"><font color=\"#444444\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span>pages_stat_subset\r\n</span>   book_id page_no views group within_group    group_name\r\n49      36       1   260     0            1 Pages [1..20]</font></pre><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;line-height:1.25;white-space:pre-wrap!important;outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;font-size:10pt!important\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;line-height:16px;border-spacing:0px\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:1.25;font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><font color=\"#444444\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span>class(pages_stat_subset)\r\n</span>[1] &quot;data.frame&quot;</font></pre></span></pre><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;line-height:1.25;white-space:pre-wrap!important;outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;font-size:10pt!important\"><font color=\"#444444\"><br></font></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0px\"><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;line-height:1.25;outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><font color=\"#444444\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span>ggplot(pages_stat_subset, aes(within_group, group_name)) + \r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre\">+ </span><span>    geom_tile(aes(fill=views)) + \r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre\">+ </span><span>    scale_x_continuous(breaks=1:pages_per_group) +\r\n</span><span style=\"white-space:pre\">+ </span><span>    scale_y_discrete(limits=rev(unique(pages_stat_subset[[&quot;group_name&quot;]])))</span></font></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;line-height:1.25;outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span><br></span></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;line-height:1.25;outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span>The plot shows correctly and the legend is present. The if I do:</span></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;;line-height:1.25;outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;font-size:10pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span><br></span></pre><pre style=\"outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all\"><span><font face=\"DejaVu Sans Mono\" color=\"#444444\"><span style=\"line-height:16.6666660308838px;white-space:pre-wrap\">&gt; pages_stat_subset[3] &lt;- 261</span></font><font face=\"DejaVu Sans Mono\" size=\"3\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"line-height:1.25;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><br></span></font></span></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all\"><span><font face=\"DejaVu Sans Mono\"><span style=\"line-height:16.6666660308838px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></font></span></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all\"><span><font face=\"DejaVu Sans Mono\"><span style=\"line-height:16.6666660308838px;white-space:pre-wrap\">and rerun the ggplot command the legend disappears. If I revert the value to 260, the legend reappears.</span></font></span></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all\"><span><font face=\"DejaVu Sans Mono\"><span style=\"line-height:16.6666660308838px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></font></span></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all\"><span><font face=\"DejaVu Sans Mono\"><span style=\"line-height:16.6666660308838px;white-space:pre-wrap\">Thanks!</span></font></span></pre><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);outline:none;border-style:none;word-break:break-all\"><span><font face=\"DejaVu Sans Mono\"><span style=\"line-height:16.6666660308838px;white-space:pre-wrap\">Rares</span></font></span></pre></span></pre></span></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
